{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion","id":910286,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Veiled Arts of Heaven : Sapphire Veil of Passion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Sidereal Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-08T13:32:48-07:00","id":910286,"title":"[Sidereals:WFHL] Veiled Arts of Heaven : Sapphire Veil of Passion","content":"(with apologies to Holden)<br /> <img src=\"https://i.ytimg.com/vi/NRnHqijV5Ck/maxresdefault.jpg\" class=\"bbcode-attachment bbcode-attachment--lightbox js-lightbox\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" itemprop=\"image\" loading=\"lazy\"/><br /> <br /> <b>SIDEREAL MARTIAL ARTS: SAPPHIRE VEIL OF PASSION</b><br /> <br /> Also known as the Twice Born Style due to having been independently discovered twice, Sapphire Veil of Passion draws inspiration from the fire of lust and passion that burns within all living beings. Many younger Sidereals make jokes (or secretly wonder) at what the training for this Veiled Art of Heaven entails, and ridicule those who devote themselves to its study. This ridicule usually lasts only until they meet with a practitioner; even the ones that don't come away half in love with the mentor that just thrashed them are forced to admit to the style's efficaciousness.<br /> <br /> <b>Weapons and armor:</b> Sapphire Veil of Passion permits the use of the Urumi, or ribbon sword, as well as the artifact equivalent, the floating ribbon. It is incompatible with armor, but does traditionally allow a buckler to be worn as well.<br /> <i>Urumi:</i> Light melee weapon; Lethal, Martial Arts, Disarming, Flexible, Reaching<br /> <i>Floating Ribbon:</i> Light artifact melee weapon; Lethal, Martial Arts, Disarming, Flexible, Reaching<br /> <i>Buckler:</i> Light melee weapon; Melee, Shield<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Satisfying Idle Fantasy</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 3m, 2i; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 1<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> None<br /> <br /> Passion begins as fantasy, which demands satisfaction. The martial artist kindles and satisfies such a fantasy in a single motion, leaving her victim stunned and confused. Satisfying Idle Fantasy may be used to enhance either a withering attack or a withering savage when in control of a grapple. The martial artist adds her Appearance to her Strength for determining raw damage. Additionally, if this attack's damage exceeds her victim's Resolve, it also instills a tie of lust or fascination towards her in him, or enhances an existing tie of the same. If her victim is crashed by an attack instilling this tie, or Satisfying Idle Fantasy is used to enhance a withering savage, the cost to resist this influence is increased to 3 willpower.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Sapphire Veil of Passion Form</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 8m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 2<br /> <b>Type:</b> Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Form<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Satisfying Idle Fantasy<br /> <br /> Assuming the Sapphire Veil of Passion Form, the martial artist kindles the blue flame of passion in her, and drawing the attention of all upon the field. Anyone who has a positive tie towards her subtracts successes equal to the rank of the tie when they take any action other than rushing or attempting to grapple her, as well as from their defense against her attacks; additionally, she gains one initiative and two additional motes per turn in which she spends at Close range with an opponent who holds a positive intimacy towards her, drawing on the strength of her enemy's ardor.<br /> <b>Special activation rules</b>: If the martial artist successfully creates or strengthens a positive tie towards herself in an enemy after joining battle, she may reflexively enter the Sapphire Veil of Passion Form.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Yellow Dragon Flight</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> (1wp); <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Dual<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sapphire Veil of Passion Form<br /> <br /> The martial artist draws on the hot, active element of sexuality, thrusting forward with an irresistible attack. Yellow Dragon Flight enhances Satisfying Idle Fantasy; by spending 1 willpower when using Satisfying Idle Fantasy, the attack also becomes unblockable and ignores soak. A successful attack enhanced by Yellow Dragon Flight against an enemy who holds a major or defining positive tie towards the martial artist awards 1 willpower.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Black Dragon Coils</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> 2m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sapphire Veil of Passion Form<br /> <br /> The martial artist draws on the cool, passive element of sexuality, accepting her opponent's attack and smothering the heat of it away. Black Dragon Flight enhances her defense; if she successfully defends herself from the attack, she steals 1 initiative from the attacker; if the attack is successful, then the martial artist may reflexively attempt to instill an intimacy of lust or facination towards her in him. Black Dragon Coil rewards two motes when the martial artist steals initiative from an enemy who holds a major or defining positive tie towards the martial artist.<br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:purple\"><b><i>Thousand Desires Ribbon</i></b></span><br /> <b>Cost:</b> (1wp); <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Yellow Dragon Flight, Black Dragon Coils<br /> <br /> The heat and the cool of the martial artist's passion combines to form a ribbon of electric blue light, arcing around them in a reflection of her thousand aching desires. When she enters Sapphire Veil of Passion Form, the martial artist may spend a point of willpower to activate Thousand Desires Ribbon. The ribbon floats and moves around the martial artist, reflecting her desires from moment to moment; each turn, the ribbon acts on the martial artist's initiative, allowing her to take one of the following actions in addition to her normal action:<br /> * She may set the ribbon to defend herself; until her next action, she gains the benefit of Black Dragon Coils on all defenses.<br /> * She may make a withering attack an enemy out to Short range; this attack is automatically enhanced with Satisfying Idle Fantasy.<br /> * She may attempt to perform a disarm, distract or grapple gambit against an enemy out to Short range.<br /> <br /> Charm usage automatically granted by the ribbon do not cost the martial artist any motes","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":169,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","user":"wastevens","date":". 06-10-2016, 08:12 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T14:21:40-07:00","id":910320,"title":"","content":"Apologies are needed for something you did wrong. You did no wrong here, so don't apologize.<ul><li>Satisfying Idle Fantasy: Why is it called dual when I see no mention for decisive attacks? 3 WP is also an awful lot to resist. I'd seriously consider putting it down to two.</li> <li>Form: I assume multiple opponents in range of this charm don't trigger this multiple times and only once right? Meaning if two opponents are in close range, than I won't gain 2i and 4m per turn right?</li> <li>Yellow Dragon: I'd probably say you'd need to beat the resolve via damage to get the WP back as otherwise it seems too trival, but I may be over-reacting.</li> <li>Black Dragon: Cost should be 2m, +1i. Fine when using charm rules involving dice caps.</li> <li>Thousand Desires Ribbon: Do these extra gambits, attacks, or automatic charm usage cost motes?</li> </ul>Overall I think this is the best SMA you did to date. As someone whose doing a ton of conversions himself, you should be really proud of this.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Read my shit at my <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/271207-sandact6-homebrew-topic\" target=\"_blank\">homebrew</a> topic, 2.5e and 3e material!<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1263020-alchemicals-2-0-3e-conversion-charm-design-request\" target=\"_blank\">Play Alchemical's in 3e now</a>, you're welcome.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1183-sandact6","name":"Sandact6","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1183_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1236"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T18:37:19-07:00","id":910461,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910320#post910320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Apologies are needed for something you did wrong. You did no wrong here, so don't apologize.</div> </div> </div> </div>More of a joke, since I know that Holden made Sapphire Veil, and is more likely to see this version than Jenna is to see the hash I'm making of her work. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910320#post910320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Satisfying Idle Fantasy: Why is it called dual when I see no mention for decisive attacks? 3 WP is also an awful lot to resist. I'd seriously consider putting it down to two.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah; it's akward, cause it only enhances withering damage, but enhances withering attacks *and* savaging when in control of a grapple for withering damage. Since grapples are started via gambit, I tend to clump them under 'decisive-only' effects. I suspect it would result in confusion either way &gt;&lt;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910320#post910320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Form: I assume multiple opponents in range of this charm don't trigger this multiple times and only once right? Meaning if two opponents are in close range, than I won't gain 2i and 4m per turn right?</div> </div> </div> </div>Correct.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910320#post910320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Yellow Dragon: I'd probably say you'd need to beat the resolve via damage to get the WP back as otherwise it seems too trival, but I may be over-reacting.</div> </div> </div> </div>I mean- I assume that in most fights, you've already had to hit them with at least 2 SIF hits, or comparable effects, to boost the tie to Major. (Plus, at the point you ignore soak, your damage is almost certainly going to be in the 5+ range anyways)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910320#post910320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Black Dragon: Cost should be 2m, +1i. Fine when using charm rules involving dice caps.</div> </div> </div> </div>*thinks*<br /> The thing is, it's not interacting with dice caps; it's sidestepping them. Rather intentionally. If I've boosted my defense to 5 and get hit by 7, I can pay 3 initative to make up the difference.<br /> <br /> In retrospect, that's too powerful. I think I'll just strip that aspect out entirely; a defensive charm that steals initative is enough.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910320#post910320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Thousand Desires Ribbon: Do these extra gambits, attacks, or automatic charm usage cost motes?</div> </div> </div> </div>Newp- the charm usages specified are free. I'll make that more explicit in the text.<br /> <br /> (That means that setting the ribbon to defense when multiple people that love you are attacking can make you powerfully mote generating- which ties back to the original form's Overdrive and all that good stuff)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sandact6</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910320#post910320\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Overall I think this is the best SMA you did to date. As someone whose doing a ton of conversions himself, you should be really proud of this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thanks <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T22:05:11-07:00","id":910567,"title":"","content":"Wow. In short, I really enjoy a lot of these ideas, and I love that this of all styles is finally getting a conversion.<br /> <br /> That said, while I love what's here, I kind of feel as if it's a little lackluster. While the 2e form was very obviously over the top, I feel like (Perhaps wrongly) That these charms, while delightful, don't add enough to stack up as a full MA form, particularly in defensive or controlling maneuvers.<br /> <br /> ...That said, I'm still totally using this, fantastic work as usual.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11609-shiney103","name":"Shiney103","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T22:09:40-07:00","id":910568,"title":"","content":"I wanna echo that I feel like this is very conceptually tight, so that's awesome! The mechanics feel clean and clear. That said...<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shiney103</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910567#post910567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That said, while I love what's here, I kind of feel as if it's a little lackluster. While the 2e form was very obviously over the top, I feel like (Perhaps wrongly) That these charms, while delightful, don't add enough to stack up as a full MA form, particularly in defensive or controlling maneuvers.</div> </div> </div> </div>I do agree with this a little bit, I think it could use a little bit... more? More of what it's got going on, but maybe some weirdness, too. I don't have any knowledge of the original form, but if it's a Sidereal Martial Art, that seems like perfect grounds for totally weird effects.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-08T23:08:38-07:00","id":910589,"title":"","content":"How powerful are SMA supposed to be, compared to Solar Charms? Black Dragon Flight seems kinda lackluster compared to Force-Stealing Feint (and is also just not very <i>interesting</i> compared to the other Charms here).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11237-jefepato","name":"Jefepato","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11237_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T05:39:21-07:00","id":910697,"title":"","content":"TL;DR: Black Dragon Coils probably got hit too hard with the nerf bat. The original form of letting you freely trade initiative to avoid getting hit was too strong, but I think I overcorrected.<br /> <br /> Maybe if you hit someone who used BDC, you have to spend a willpower or develop an intimacy?<br /> <br /> Long form;<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shiney103</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910567#post910567\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. In short, I really enjoy a lot of these ideas, and I love that this of all styles is finally getting a conversion.<br /> <br /> That said, while I love what's here, I kind of feel as if it's a little lackluster. While the 2e form was very obviously over the top, I feel like (Perhaps wrongly) That these charms, while delightful, don't add enough to stack up as a full MA form, particularly in defensive or controlling maneuvers.<br /> <br /> ...That said, I'm still totally using this, fantastic work as usual.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910568#post910568\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I wanna echo that I feel like this is very conceptually tight, so that's awesome! The mechanics feel clean and clear. That said...<br /> <br /> I do agree with this a little bit, I think it could use a little bit... more? More of what it's got going on, but maybe some weirdness, too. I don't have any knowledge of the original form, but if it's a Sidereal Martial Art, that seems like perfect grounds for totally weird effects.</div> </div> </div> </div><div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Jefepato</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910589#post910589\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How powerful are SMA supposed to be, compared to Solar Charms? Black Dragon Flight seems kinda lackluster compared to Force-Stealing Feint (and is also just not very <i>interesting</i> compared to the other Charms here).</div> </div> </div> </div>Warning- long post is long and goes into brain space detail.<br /> <br /> As an internally imposed constraint, WFHL SMA styles are (by their nature) shorter than original styles. In compensation, for power scaling, they're intended to be 'pushed' for their Essence minimums; they should be roughly 1.5 Essence ahead of the curve.<br /> <br /> Here's my notes/summary of the original style's charms:<ul><li> Into Infinite Depths: Learn a fucking lot about someone</li> <li> Eternal Infatuation Dance: Perfect dodge &amp; move to close range of attacker, rush enhancer, once per scene</li> <li> Yellow Dragon Flight: Unblockable, unsoakable attack that ignites victim\u2019s essence</li> <li> Black Dragon Coils: Perfect parry, restores (virtue channels? willpower?)</li> <li> Dissolution of Virtue: Until you move, do not suffer penalties to defense</li> <li> Satisfying Idle Fantasy: Attacks impose or enhance positive intimacies towards you</li> <li> Sapphire Veil of Passion Form: Gain protection from intimacies others hold towards you, regenerate Essence quickly</li> <li> Someone Else\u2019s Consequences: Reflexively terminate Psyche, Poison or Disease, transferring them to a victim.</li> <li> Silken Rope Trick: Red Rule Violation: The Charm</li> <li> Joy in Ownership: Trap someone with defining intimacy to love and obey, pysche</li> <li> Sapphire Binding Pattern: Seriously, you win grapples forever</li> <li> Memories of Intimacy: Make an attack unblockable and undodgable against someone you have beaten, who has an intimacy towards you, or whom you own.</li> <li> Thousand Desires Ribbon: Supercharge Form; reflexive attacks, out to short range, increase severity of wound penalties</li> </ul><br /> <br /> In early tinkering with the style, I decided I wanted Sapphire Veil to focus on withering / initiative control, as compared with the more decisive focus that Charcoal March of Spiders had.<br /> I also decided that focusing on exploiting intimacies others have towards you would be a sufficiently rich region to mine.<br /> I also wanted SVoD to be a more traditionally structured style- having a Form and a capstone (as compared with the all forms PAoC and incomplete CMoS.) <br /> (CMoS and SVoD are both probably the most 'normal' SMAs- and as a consequence, the conversation of both comes across as the most down to earth. The big piece of weirdness from CMoS, independent actions, is getting eaten by OSoI)<br /> <br /> Of the original charms...<br /> <br /> * Dissolution of Virtue and Into Infinite Depths got cut for being out out of theme.<br /> * Silken Rope Trick got cut for being Red Rule Violation: The Charm<br /> <br /> * Satisfying Idle Fantasy served as an excellent entry into the style.<br /> * Yellow Dragon Flight and Black Dragon Coils worked well with the ideas of the style, as well as mirroring one another.<br /> <br /> That left the Form and a capstone.<br /> <br /> * Someone Else's Consequence, Eternal Infatuation Dance, and Sapphire Binding Pattern didn't feel like capstones.<br /> <br /> That left Joy in Ownership, Memories of Intimacy, and Thousand Desires Ribbon as potential capstones.<br /> <br /> I ruled out Memories of Intimacy as being kind of win-more (unblockable attack against someone you've already beaten) or redundent with Yellow Dragon Flight- that left Joy in Ownership and Thousand Desires Ribbon.<br /> <br /> When I saw the Form's overdrive mote generation, that pushed me to thinking of SVoD as also being incredibly generative- which echoes on the theme of desire and sexuality.<br /> <br /> Joy in Ownership wants to be a finishing move- a decisive only gambit you use to trap someone into being enthralled by you. Thousand Desires Ribbon wants to be a form enhancer, accentuating the generative qualities of the style.<br /> <br /> I decided that, between the two, Joy in Ownership would generate more bad feelings of loss of player agency and trouble with creating an army of lovesick thralls, whereas Thousand Ribbons Desire could be made pure upside.<br /> <br /> So- thus, selected. From there, it just became a matter of finding the right inspiration for the particulars.<br /> <br /> Now- all that said -Black Dragon Coils probably got hit too hard with the nerf bat. The original form of letting you freely trade initiative to avoid getting hit was too strong, but I think I overcorrected.<br /> <br /> Maybe if you hit someone who used BDC, you have to spend a willpower or develop an intimacy?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T07:40:05-07:00","id":910774,"title":"","content":"(Also, Obsidian Shards of Infinity is going to notably up to 'pushing the weirdness and power' quotients)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T10:20:28-07:00","id":910921,"title":"","content":"I absolutely won't pretend to have the knowhow or balancing intuition you do, looking forward to seeing how this turns out. Thankfully, I'm glad this tree exists at all, as it is basically &quot;Red Rule Violation - The MA Form.&quot; So it seems like cutting and clipping the style based on that doesn't make much sense. but hey, if it gets it allowed at more tables, who am I to complain?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11609-shiney103","name":"Shiney103","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T11:16:03-07:00","id":910973,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wastevens</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910697#post910697\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Maybe if you hit someone who used BDC, you have to spend a willpower or develop an intimacy?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think that's a cool idea.<br /> <br /> What if the style's intimacy based effects scale based on whether it's minor or Major? So if it's a Minor intimacy for say, Sapphire Veil of Passion Form, you gain the 1 Initiative and 2 motes, and if its a Major Intimacy, maybe 1 auto-success? It'd make it easier to hit someone <i>and </i>you might be able to convince them to stop fighting at all.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of a fan of Stupid Sexy Flanders style, to be honest.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T11:27:36-07:00","id":910983,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Leetsepeak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=910973#post910973\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think that's a cool idea.<br /> <br /> What if the style's intimacy based effects scale based on whether it's minor or Major? So if it's a Minor intimacy for say, Sapphire Veil of Passion Form, you gain the 1 Initiative and 2 motes, and if its a Major Intimacy, maybe 1 auto-success? It'd make it easier to hit someone <i>and </i>you might be able to convince them to stop fighting at all.<br /> <br /> I'm kind of a fan of Stupid Sexy Flanders style, to be honest.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Form actually did scale based on intimacy strength (and so did all the charms, at one point!), but I decided to strike it for two reasons;<br /> A) It added a non-trivial amount of complexity for a very modest gain in difference in feeling during play.<br /> B) It revealed information that would normally require a Read Intentions to get.<br /> <br /> The current approach still bumps into B- pretty much anything that's going to tie into intimacies will! But making things binary do/don't apply both reduces the information and the complexity. Seems worth it to me. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> That said- I'm playing with bumping Black Dragon Coils being another intimacy builder.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-09T11:29:47-07:00","id":910985,"title":"","content":"Yeah, I think that makes sense, especially with the binary approach.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I am no longer participating in the community. Please do not contact me about my previous work.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/159-leetsepeak","name":"Leetsepeak","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4259"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T00:12:26-07:00","id":911508,"title":"","content":"After a brief discussion with our fine writer here, I've decided to try and make a few other homebrew charms to 'tack on.' These are meant to make the SVoP style function more autonomously/more similar to it's 2e form, and as such, should be considered carefully before being allowed into your game, or used with other MA abilities, as this can easily shatter your balance harder than a <b>Glorious Solar Homebrew Technique</b><br /> <br /> That said, I could still use some feedback moving things into 3E style.<br /> <br /> <b>SIDEREAL MARTIAL ARTS: SAPPHIRE VEIL OF PASSION: <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><i>RUBY RIBBON EXPANSION</i></span></b><br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Eternal Infatuation Dance</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>6m, 1WP; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 3<br /> <b>Type:</b> Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Perilous<br /> <b>Duration: </b>Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Yellow Dragon Flight<br /> <br /> The martial artist draws on what she has learned from the heat of passion, and of the weaknesses it creates in others. Once per Scene, this Charm may be activated in response to any single attack the martial artist is aware of. The martial artist vanishes in a swirl of collapsing sapphire ribbons, appearing in the close range band of her attacker. In the case of long-range social attacks, this Charm\u2019s maximum range is (Essencex5) Miles. This traditionally avoids all effects of the initial attack, but the movement offers no protection against hazards where she appears. This charm cannot be reset via normal means.<br /> <br /> An Essence 5 repurchase allows this charm to maintain the proximity: As long as the martial artist does not intentionally move away from her target, she may stay in the close range band, regardless of natural or supernatural movement capabilities employed by her target.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Authors thoughts: I liked the idea of an emergency defense, but there wasn't a single aspect I wasn't okay with turning down, as it technically is a once-per-scene perfect defense, so far as I can tell. Additionally, the unshakeable pursuit option sounded nice, so I moved that to an E5 repurchase. </div> </div> </div><b>Silken Rope trick</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>10m; 1WP <b>Mins: </b>Essence 4<br /> <b>Type:</b> Reflexive<br /> <b>Keywords</b>: Perilous, Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> One Scene<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Sapphire Veil of Passion Form, Black Dragon Coils<br /> <br /> While in the Sapphire Veil of Passion Form, the Martial Artist gains additional insight into passion itself, and how it can be manipulated by those with the skill to do so. The martial artist may activate this charm when attempting to make a grapple, or in response to another attempting to enter a grapple with her. She is unable to make Rush or Disengage actions while this Charm is in effect. More beneficially, she adds her Appearance rating in dice to attempts to establish or maintain a grapple. Additionally, anyone who enters a grapple with the martial artist, must immediately pay one willpower, or instils a tie of lust towards her in the attacker, or enhances an existing tie of the same.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Authors thoughts: <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Red Rule violation: The Charm. </b></span>Obviously, this isn't acceptable at some tables, and if so, that's fine. However it exists as another means to instil and strengthen intimacies, but with a fairly high cost and pre-requisite to try and offset the idea. </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> <br /> <b>Thousand Desires Ribbon <span style=\"color:#B22222\">((Minor Addendum))</span></b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>1wp; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 4<br /> <b>Type: </b>Permanent<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Permanent<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms: </b>Yellow Dragon Flight, Black Dragon Coils<br /> <br /> The heat and the cool of the martial artist's passion combines to form a ribbon of electric blue light, arcing around them in a reflection of her thousand aching desires. When she enters Sapphire Veil of Passion Form, the martial artist may spend a point of willpower to activate Thousand Desires Ribbon. The ribbon floats and moves around the martial artist, reflecting her desires from moment to moment; each turn, the ribbon acts on the martial artist's initiative, allowing her to take one of the following actions in addition to her normal action:<br /> <br /> * She may set the ribbon to defend herself; until her next action, she gains the benefit of Black Dragon Coils on all defenses.<br /> * She may make a withering attack an enemy out to Short range; this attack is automatically enhanced with Satisfying Idle Fantasy.<br /> * She may attempt to perform a disarm, distract or grapple gambit against an enemy out to Short range. <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>Grapples made with this attack may be enhanced by Silken Rope Trick as normal, but the user must still activate the charm as normal for the bonus to apply.</b></span><br /> <br /> Charms specified by the action taken with the ribbon do not cost the martial artist any motes.<br /> <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>An Essence 5 repurchase will allow the Martial artist to spend an additional willpower when activating the form, allowing one additional action. This cannot be enhanced further.</b></span><br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Authors thoughts: Fine as it is, but wanted to clear up no silken rope freebies. I also wanted to add in the ability for an E5 repurchase to make this power capable of more, but ultimately, this isn't what I consider the real strength of the form. </div> </div> </div><b>Joy In Ownership</b><br /> <b>Cost: </b>20m, 2WP; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 5<br /> <b>Type: </b>Simple<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> Psyche<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Thousand Desires Ribbon, Eternal Infatuation Dance, Silken Rope Trick<br /> <br /> The martial artist has learned what is assumed to be every appreciable aspect of passion, and as such, can enforce it's mantra with utmost potency upon the undefended. The martial artist must touch an individual whom is unconscious, or made so by the martial artist. If the subject has a major or defining positive tie towards the martial artist, with a significant effort, she can further reinforce this, creating a new defining intimacy of &quot;Love and Obey.&quot; This unnatural mental influence can be resisted only by spending an amount of willpower equal to the target's essence. Otherwise, it must be weakened and removed in a manner similar to other intimacies. While this intimacy is in effect however, other positive intimacies towards the martial artist cannot be weakened or removed short of unnatural mental influence.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Author Thoughts: Woo, silken rope trick was bad? Controversy out the wazoo in a single charm. That said, I've discussed this with some players, who consider this to be the true 'capstone.' of the style. While I disagree, I can see why it's considered to be an iconic element thereof. I might make this Essence ??? And require a special Essence 6+ teacher to learn. that said, I've bumped up the cost, and allowed it to function a little less like a slavery charm, and more like a knot to hold the other intimacies in place. No memory rewrites, no metaphysical slavery, no multi-scene willpower expenditure. </div> </div> </div><b>Memories of Intimacy</b><br /> <b>Cost: 4</b>m; <b>Mins:</b> Essence 5<br /> <b>Type: </b>Supplemental<br /> <b>Keywords:</b> None<br /> <b>Duration:</b> Instant<br /> <b>Prerequisite Charms:</b> Joy In Ownership<br /> <br /> The martial artist is an undisputed master of passion, and any affected by her passing are affected by it, often never able to completely overcome the memories and the effects they have on them. This charm supplements a Martial Arts attack, rendering it both unblockable and undodgeable if any of the following apply:<ul><li>The martial artist has defeated the target in combat at some point in the past (defined as having rendered the target unconscious, or the target having voluntarily admitted defeat or surrendered to the martial artist on the field of battle, even if only in a sparring match).</li> <li>The target carries an Intimacy of any sort for the martial artist.</li> <li>The Martial artist successfully performs a disarm, distract, or unhorse gambit against the target in the same scene.</li> </ul>If two or more of these criteria apply to the target, the attack is also considered unexpected. Memories of Intimacy may only be used once per scene, but may be reset by increasing the strength of an intimacy held towards you.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Author thoughts: Here we are. What I consider to be the capstone of the style, is that recurring fights become very dangerous. Aside from a little trimming related to the controversial charms above, I actually felt this charm was too expensive for a single attack booster in Ex3, and shaved three motes off the cost. That said, this is something I'm not quite sure how it affects balance, as unblockable/undodgeable attacks have been nonexistent in my games so far. </div> </div> </div><br /> Summary: A lot of these could be particularly powerful. but by splattering it with the psyche and perilous keywords where I thought appropriate, it makes a master of the SVoP style singularly deadly, if not by the traditional means, which is exactly what I think a Sideral Master should be. That said, this absolutely reeks of controversial tones, and has only had the most basic of once-overs for balance, so revisions will definitely be forthcoming.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":11609,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11609-shiney103","user":"Shiney103","date":". 06-11-2016, 05:02 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11609-shiney103","name":"Shiney103","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T05:35:55-07:00","id":911586,"title":"","content":"So, question for evaluation purposes;<br /> Are you operating on the original paradigm of unlimited access to Sidereal Martial Arts charms, pending Essence prereqs and having a complete Celestial Martial Art mastered, or under my paradigm of limited access to the number of Sidereal Martial Arts charms, but easier access for those that can be reached.<br /> <br /> For the moment, I'm going to assume the former, cause otherwise this style is just too fat now.<br /> <br /> Also, as a general note- the new charms are not cohesively integrated. Eternal Infatuation Dance branching from Yellow Dragon Flight is perfectly cromulent; I'd add Silken Rope Trick as branching from Black Dragon Coils, and then make Joy in Ownership require Eternal Infatuation Dance, Silken Rope Trick, and Thousand Desires Ribbon, with Memories of Intimacy requireing Joy in Ownership.<br /> <br /> \u200b<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shiney103</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=911508#post911508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> Eternal Infatuation Dance</b></div> </div> </div> </div>The cost implies that there is an optional willpower cost for Eternal Infatuation Dance, but the conditions under which it is spent or to what effect. And, as a technical matter, 'allow a roll to avoid or defend against' is not a great piece of terminology, since few defenses are active in that sense now. Also, does this work on written social attacks? That's a kind of... strange mental image.<br /> <br /> Finally, I'm a *little* dubious about repurchases in martial arts trees, since they reduce the cohesive 'wholeness' of the tree. None of the published MA styles have repurchase effects, and I doubt that's on accident.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shiney103</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=911508#post911508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Silken Rope trick</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Again with the seemingly optional willpower cost.<br /> Otherwise this seems tolerable. Allowing the intimacy to be resisted via willpower goes a long way to mitigating the red rule violation nature of the original.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shiney103</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=911508#post911508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">* She may attempt to perform a disarm, distract or grapple gambit against an enemy out to Short range. <span style=\"color:#B22222\"><b>This does not automatically activate Silken Rope Trick, but the user may pay the additional cost to activate the charm if applicable.</b></span></div> </div> </div> </div>What additional cost? Silken Rope Trick is a scenelong enhancement; do I have to activate it distinctly for my ribbon? For every grapple I attempt with the ribbon?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shiney103</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=911508#post911508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> Joy In Ownership</b></div> </div> </div> </div>Imma side with the majority; this feels more like the capstone of the style if it exists. That said, I like this approach of making an intimacy that ties up other intimacies.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shiney103</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=911508#post911508\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b> Memories of Intimacy</b></div> </div> </div> </div>'Any sort of intimacy' is probably too strong now- especially considering that the other effects in the style key off of Major or greater intimacies.<br /> <br /> Also, I feel like 12m is too expensive, unless you're also bringing the Sutra effects / discounts back in.<br /> <br /> Mostly, I feel like this is a charm that can too easily engender bad feelings and frustrations in players. Either it renders previously defeated opponents trivial (which reduces the ability to reuse antagonists), or is too expensive to use (which makes it frustrating to have purchased). And, on an antagonist figure, it either makes them unfairly potent (which makes them less fun to fight) or, again, is too expensive (which makes it a bit of a trap for an unwary ST)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-10T08:43:19-07:00","id":911683,"title":"","content":"Wow, I must have been not thinking at all when I was formatting that. Let me make some corrections, and take you through it. <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Are you operating on the original paradigm of unlimited access to Sidereal Martial Arts charms, pending Essence prereqs and having a complete Celestial Martial Art mastered, or under my paradigm of limited access to the number of Sidereal Martial Arts charms, but easier access for those that can be reached.<br /> <br /> For the moment, I'm going to assume the former, cause otherwise this style is just too fat now. </div> </div> </div>I'm developing the former, as I mentioned, my goal was to make it a more 'fat' as you put it, MA that stands with full functionality on it's own, rather than limiting the number of sidereal Martial arts. Mostly because, I'm honestly unsure how to make the attempt to balance it by the latter's standards, and really wanted to cherry pick a few things I thought the style lacked in order to stand on it's own. As I'm not an expert, my point of reference was to take an existing 3E MA core tree, and compare it for balance, and be able to say &quot;I'm not sure which of these I'd rather fight.&quot; <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Also, as a general note- the new charms are not cohesively integrated. Eternal Infatuation Dance branching from Yellow Dragon Flight is perfectly cromulent; I'd add Silken Rope Trick as branching from Black Dragon Coils, and then make Joy in Ownership require Eternal Infatuation Dance, Silken Rope Trick, and Thousand Desires Ribbon, with Memories of Intimacy requireing Joy in Ownership. </div> </div> </div>I'll run through and re-update that. The pre-reqs was an area that I planned to view better with a set of visual aids for the tree.... That I went and forgot about. Whoops. I'll modify them based on your reccomendations, but have a comment about capstones in the relevant charm.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Finally, I'm a *little* dubious about repurchases in martial arts trees, since they reduce the cohesive 'wholeness' of the tree. None of the published MA styles have repurchase effects, and I doubt that's on accident </div> </div> </div>Totally, understandable. When I was designing these trees, charms, it felt like some parts of them would be too powerful, yet otherwise, would lose some of the mystical power that makes them so bizarre and enchanting. My compromise, was to allow a higher essence repurchase of the charms, to 'refine' the technique, or unlock it's true potential. a common trope in source material, but like you mentioned, completely absent in the core rules. Basically, it was the only compromise I could find that made sense. Someone truly dedicated to the wacky weirdness would be able to drop more experience on strange esoteric martial prowess, yet it was by no means neccesary to fill out and practice the style prior to super high essence gameplay.<br /> <br /> <b>On Eternal Infatuation Dance, </b>(And the rest of the charms) I formatted the flat out willpower cost, as an optional willpower cost. Whoops. Not a lot to say about that, but I've fixed it. As for some of the wording, it's a mix between trying to use the 'common sense language' and a lot of the exact wording from the 2E style. That said, I've just tried to re-word it to read better, and remove the reference to blatant social attacks, though that was lifted right out of the 2E charm description.<br /> <br /> <br /> <b>On Silken Rope Trick,</b> I formatted the willpower cost incorrectly, it's not optional. As for using it with the ribbon, I'll re-word my text. After finally getting some sleep, the idea behind it was to explain that SRT could be used with ribbon grapples, but was not automatically/freely enhanced by it, you would have to activate the charm for the scene, as usual. Re-worded for clarity. <br /> <br /> <b>On Joy In Ownership,</b> Well, see- Wait, what? You're okay with this? I had imagined this of all things, would be me fighting an uphill battle both ways to try and make this a thing. That said, I held an unusual mentality towards capstones. They should be singularly powerful, define some of what the style is about, and make those who wield it feel pretty good about it. Unfortunately, in my (admittedly small) test group, there were two philosophies about what made SVoP great. One theory was the 'creating people strongly tied to you.' While the other was 'Making Recurring fights extremely difficult. So onwards to....<br /> <br /> <b>Memories of Intimacy</b> was intended to tone down the overwhelming power somewhat, but still allow a master of the form to function much more powerfully against those they've already crossed. My idea was to make it so that each attack enhanced in this way would be powerful, but singularly expensive. It's clear that a 'dual capstone' won't work on this style, and I'd love some input on trying to make this design philosophy work. Otherwise, it might be best to scrap this charm, despite the interesting flavor it has.<br /> <br /> <b>In summary:</b> Whoops, made some silly mistakes there. Formatting correct, pre-reqs adjusted, wording and language cleared up. Surprised how little seemed to be against balance. Like I said, though, I'd love some design input on the shakier things I've suggested, such as the repurchase, or the capstone issue in general.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11609-shiney103","name":"Shiney103","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T06:20:28-07:00","id":912208,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shiney103</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=911683#post911683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>On Joy In Ownership,</b> Well, see- Wait, what? You're okay with this? I had imagined this of all things, would be me fighting an uphill battle both ways to try and make this a thing. That said, I held an unusual mentality towards capstones. They should be singularly powerful, define some of what the style is about, and make those who wield it feel pretty good about it. Unfortunately, in my (admittedly small) test group, there were two philosophies about what made SVoP great. One theory was the 'creating people strongly tied to you.' While the other was 'Making Recurring fights extremely difficult. So onwards to....</div> </div> </div> </div>My main reason for calling Joy in Ownership 'Red Rule Violation: The Charm' from the original style was because it was *such* a powerful effect and completely irresitable, without the subject's prior mental state or ability to resist factored in. Your version instead enhances an existing intimacy, and does a clever thing with the intimacy system (the 'protective' intimacy idea).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shiney103</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=911683#post911683\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>Memories of Intimacy</b> was intended to tone down the overwhelming power somewhat, but still allow a master of the form to function much more powerfully against those they've already crossed. My idea was to make it so that each attack enhanced in this way would be powerful, but singularly expensive. It's clear that a 'dual capstone' won't work on this style, and I'd love some input on trying to make this design philosophy work. Otherwise, it might be best to scrap this charm, despite the interesting flavor it has.</div> </div> </div> </div>The *easiest* way would be to put a 'once a scene' limit, and then knock the cost from 12m to like, 4m. Have a reset condition of 'increasing the strength of an intimacy the victim of the attack holds towards you' or some such. Get rid of the crippling effect clause (that's not a well defined concept in E3), and put a time limit on the 'time since last defeated'- defeated within the past year or somesuch. Maybe make it Withering-only, to contrast with Black Claw Style's super deadly capstone.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T06:43:03-07:00","id":912216,"title":"","content":"Wow. Again, for someone who will gladly call themselves a total rookie, I'm amazed at how well this is seeming to turn out. I'm editing my earlier post currently, to reflect some of the suggested changes. considering the circumstances of Memories of intimacy requiring an intimacy or a defeat in the first place. resetting it becomes difficult, for most fights, short of attacking someone who holds none, which is awesome. MY biggest concern, is now there are only two items which could allow the charm to apply, and I'd like for the list to be at least three long, any ideas there?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11609-shiney103","name":"Shiney103","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T08:27:08-07:00","id":912249,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shiney103</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/sidereal-exalted/910286-sidereals-wfhl-veiled-arts-of-heaven-sapphire-veil-of-passion?p=912216#post912216\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wow. Again, for someone who will gladly call themselves a total rookie, I'm amazed at how well this is seeming to turn out. I'm editing my earlier post currently, to reflect some of the suggested changes. considering the circumstances of Memories of intimacy requiring an intimacy or a defeat in the first place. resetting it becomes difficult, for most fights, short of attacking someone who holds none, which is awesome. MY biggest concern, is now there are only two items which could allow the charm to apply, and I'd like for the list to be at least three long, any ideas there?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Don't assume that I know what the hell I'm talking about <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> I've been tinkering with Exalted since 1E, and believe I have a tolerably good set of bowel cognition, but when you start to use any homebrew material at a table, be very sensitive to unintended consequences and player response.<br /> <br /> Re: Third condition- maybe someone you have successfully disarmed, distracted, or crashed in the scene? That's a kind of small scale defeat that feels appropriate for the style.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My Storyteller Vault releases!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/269728/Sorcerous-Ways-Mystic-Martial-Arts\" target=\"_blank\">Sorcerous Ways: Mystic Martial Arts</a> - Punch people for magic power!<br /> <a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/product/252892/These-Mean-Streets\" target=\"_blank\">These Mean Streets</a> - Advise and systems for street-level punk-noir Vampire larp","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/169-wastevens","name":"wastevens","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar169_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"939"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-11T14:00:39-07:00","id":912422,"title":"","content":"While I've designed and tweaked and balanced the D20 system in various forms for over a decade, I'm not even into my third year with exalted. Thanks for the information, and as always, any homebrew must be accepted as having the potential to disrupt the game and be removed, no matter how painstakingly you try to balance it. (Happens with the official rules too, we cry and call it &quot;Errata&quot;)<br /> <br /> Thanks for the tip, I'll finalize that, and, I think my work on the controversial expansion is finished. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/cool.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Cool\" smilieid=\"6\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11609-shiney103","name":"Shiney103","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"41"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}